id: pm-uey8od
title: "Probabilistic delivery forecasting: calibrated completion-date distributions for every milestone, sampled from recorded throughput and the dependency graph"
description: "Monte Carlo forecasting over empirical throughput, the open dependency graph, reference-class conditioning, and modeled scope growth, producing P50/P85/P95 completion ranges per milestone plus a calibration ledger that scores every past forecast against what actually happened."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 3
tags[5]: analytics,"area:graph","area:sdk",governance,planning
created_at: "2026-07-25T17:48:39.569Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-25T17:59:12.018Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: "Forecasts are computed from immutable history alone (throughput sampled from real completion events, never from estimated_minutes as a basis); output is a distribution with P50/P85/P95 per milestone or subtree, never a single date; the simulation walks blocked_by/parent edges so dependency serialization is reflected; sampling is conditioned by reference class (type/tag/parent) with documented back-off to the global class when a class is sparse; modeled scope growth is included as a sampled variable; every published forecast is recorded and scored against the realized outcome, and the calibration hit rate is queryable; raw simulation rows are available as NDJSON for jq; computation is built on promoted SDK primitives and surfaced through the existing pm-brief package, adding no core command"
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: medium
confidence: medium
